  "notes": [
    "regions are anchored to the fitted dike: s along strike (NNW positive, the U\u2225 sign convention), t perpendicular (ENE positive); north half 0 < s < L/2, south half -L/2 < s < 0",
    "model_mean_cm is the uniform-opening fit referenced like the observations (per-geometry LOS, per-dataset far-field reference plane, same solve and rotation) over the same cells; the plane is fitted at cell resolution, an approximation to the native-pixel referencing worth about 0.2 cm in the contrasts; model_raw_mean_cm is the unreferenced elastic displacement, kept for comparison",
    "formal sigmas assume independent cells; the control-box scatter is a correlated-noise floor, not a demonstrated error model \u2014 the boxes sit almost entirely east of the dike; closure (closure_median_sigma_units) measures cross-sensor consistency only, so its match to the west-flank regions makes the floor plausible there without certifying it, east-flank errors certainly exceed the floor, and sigma-unit statements are ratios to the floor, not established significances",
    "individual half means are strike-dependent (the WEST south mean moves from -4.2 to -0.4 cm under the alternative strike); the north-minus-south contrast is the resolved, strike-robust quantity, not the southward motion of a single half",
    "a strike error leaks U\u22a5 into U\u2225 with one sign per flank, shifting both halves of a flank together; the north-minus-south differential is the strike-robust statistic (see strike_sensitivity)",
    "max_single_cell_influence_cm is the largest change of a differential when any single cell is removed; the EAST differential is fragile by this measure, the WEST one is not"
